Package: TALOS
Type: Package
Title: Tandem duplication detection via Alignment-free Lookup Of Skipped k-mers
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Firstname", family = "Lavauxt",
             role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "lavauxt@example.com")
Description: TALOS detects internal tandem duplications (ITDs) and partial tandem
    duplications (PTDs) in genes like FLT3 and KMT2A directly from BAM files using
    a fast, alignment-free k-mer breakpoint algorithm with sequence collapse
    optimization. It outputs HGVS-compliant cDNA and protein annotations, VCF/TSV
    reports, and PDF visualizations. A bundled static hotspot CSV (built from
    Ensembl/UCSC coordinates) allows annotation against known coding variant
    regions; users may optionally build an up-to-date SQLite database from Ensembl
    via update_hotspot_db(). This version includes memory-optimized vectorized
    sequence extraction, BSgenome caching, and raw-byte k-matching for
    significantly improved speed and RAM usage.
